e access, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior same: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 writes body without setting Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact response bodies? Same status codes, same response bodies. For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n? Go map keys sorted alphabetically: email then name. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and w.Write, no trailing newline. That would change body. Need use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode for success to preserve newline. Or write exact? Better keep encoder.\n\n", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0030493689700961113], [760, -6.889895915985107]], [[1144, -1.5497327694902197e-05], [14235, -11.867704391479492]], [[4087, -0.015473675914108753], [310, -4.359157085418701]], [[1156, -0.03197545185685158], [303, -3.7608554363250732]], [[579, -0.21897076070308685], [25, -2.32179594039917]], [[1622, -0.003213736228644848], [3296, -6.47459602355957]], [[13, -0.3743092715740204], [25, -1.5128438472747803]], [[14235, -0.03284479305148125], [1165, -4.143564701080322]], [[89109, -0.3200315535068512], [7936, -1.8540700674057007]], [[5805, -0.00023182934091892093], [2400, -8.813965797424316]], [[9830, -0.026759237051010132], [6795, -3.685797691345215]], [[6795, -2.9802766221109778e-05], [17369, -11.938841819763184]], [[1083, -1.377699613571167], [47781, -1.5678316354751587]], [[1228, -0.10003272444009781], [2400, -2.7614667415618896]], [[470, -3.230623769923113e-05], [5568, -10.619087219238281]], [[5568, -0.003135166596621275], [74243, -6.088305950164795]], [[440, -0.9291600584983826], [25, -1.900837779045105]], [[2